        "id": "kestrel-overnight",
        "heading": "One night on battery: a low-battery alert and a package alert",
        "text": [
          "Thursday night into Friday morning with the Kestrel Porch Cam, a battery doorbell camera with a small solar panel. Every 30 minutes the camera checks in with Kestrel (battery level, charging or not), and the Kestrel app shows the latest check-in. Choose **Normal morning** or **Wi-Fi down at delivery** to see the two ways the morning can end.",
          "Source: the reviewed Kestrel Porch Cam overnight design and the product manager's answers. The date, exact minutes, the check-in times between shown moments and the solar charge rate used (3% per hour, the low end of the design's 3–4%) are illustrative.",
          "The requested times and the design's power figures disagree: at about 1% per hour, plus 1% for the raccoon clip, the battery would reach 20% around 2:30 AM, not 4:00 AM. The page keeps the requested 4:00 AM alert, so the battery is shown holding at 25% until the 4:00 AM check-in reports 20%."
        ],
